    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 all 14 tests pass, including the two new `Cp07Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented server-side defaulting of the owner's registration date, returned as an ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` string on `POST /api/owners` and `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` property (`type: string`, `format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Because `Owner` composes `OwnerFields` via `allOf`, this makes the field available on both the request DTO (`OwnerFieldsDto`) and the response DTO (`OwnerDto`), and `format: date` generates a `LocalDate` that Jackson serializes/parses as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (entity) \u2014 added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field mapped to a `registration_date` column, with getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps it by name in both directions (request\u2192entity, entity\u2192response), so a supplied date round-trips unchanged.\n\n3. **DB schemas** \u2014 added a `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table in all four schema files (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres); tests run against hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column had to be declared explicitly.\n\n4. **`DefaultRegistrationDate`** (new OfficeFloor function) + wiring in **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 a small step inserted between `build` and `save` that stamps `LocalDate.now()` when the client supplied no date, and leaves a supplied date untouched. It mutates the entity in place via `@Val`, under the same `transaction` governance as the surrounding steps.\n\nThe update (`PUT`) path deliberately doesn't touch `registrationDate`, so `ApplyOwner` mutating the loaded entity preserves the stored date.",
